% SPDX-License-Identifier: GFDL-1.3-or-later
% Copyright The WP43 and C47 Authors
%
% c47appnote -- the shared design language for C47/R47 application notes.
%
% Compiled with lualatex. Consolidates the keypress and screen notation that AN0029, AN0030 and AN0031
% each carried inline, the palette they share, the page geometry, the running heads, the callout
% blocks, the listing and table styles and the two keyboard maps. A note that loads this package needs
% a four-line preamble.
%
% Package options
%   nofonts     do not touch the fonts; the note sets its own
%   serifmath   leave mathematics in the default face instead of matching the sans body
%
% Fonts. Body and headings are TeX Gyre Heros, the metric-compatible Helvetica that ships with TeX Live,
% so every contributor gets the same page. Mathematics is New Computer Modern Sans Math, also from
% TeX Live, so a variable matches the prose around it rather than falling back to a serif. The display
% face is JuliaMono, which is not in TeX Live: install it and the screen and program boxes reproduce the
% calculator glyph for glyph, and without it the package falls back to DejaVu Sans Mono and warns.
%
% THREE RULES HOLD THE DESIGN TOGETHER. Break any of them and the notes stop looking like one another.
%
%   1. fcol and gcol mean "reached through the f shift" and "reached through the g shift". Nothing
%      else may use them: not a heading, not a rule, not a running head, not a callout.
%
%   2. A filled panel is the calculator's own screen. \screen and \prog carry the lcdbg wash because
%      they reproduce the display. Everything else -- tables, listings, callouts -- is unfilled and
%      bounded by hairlines, so a fill on the page always means the same thing.
%
%   3. Rules carry weight in one direction only: 1pt closes the masthead, 0.7pt opens and closes a
%      table, 0.4pt is every other hairline. No double rules and no vertical rules anywhere.
%
%   4. A chart tells its series apart by dash pattern and marker, not by hue. Rule 1 leaves almost no
%      hue space: orange and blue are the shifts and red is the warning accent, and exactly one further
%      hue clears all three under protanopia, deuteranopia, tritanopia and normal vision. It is
%      chartink, and a chart gets at most that one. See the Charts section below for the arithmetic.

\NeedsTeXFormat{LaTeX2e}
\ProvidesPackage{c47appnote}[2026/07/29 v1.1 C47/R47 application note design language]

\newif\ifcan@fonts    \can@fontstrue
\newif\ifcan@sansmath \can@sansmathtrue
\DeclareOption{nofonts}{\can@fontsfalse}
\DeclareOption{serifmath}{\can@sansmathfalse}
\DeclareOption*{\PackageWarning{c47appnote}{Unknown option '\CurrentOption'}}
\ProcessOptions\relax

\RequirePackage{iftex}
\RequireLuaTeX

% A 1.25 in margin puts the measure near 75 characters, which is the usual readability target, and
% leaves the keyboard maps room to sit at close to their natural width.
\RequirePackage[letterpaper, margin=1.25in]{geometry}

